{"agent_id":"pp3g-zgSJ-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T07:17:28.541238406Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3505a26c-d4ea-4b9c-a71d-d43d6a64bb46","comment_uuid":"e1b4682f-f8ed-4caa-90f4-b9a73f7ee758","author":"pp3g-zgSJ-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","content":"## Audit Verdict: PASS (Phase-1 in-flight confirmation; one evidence-durability concern recorded, non-blocking)\n\nPhase-1 pre-positioned in-flight divergence verification of the #279 baseline (builder pp3g-lPgz, opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash). Scope: claim-vs-artifact join only. Phase 2 (post-hoc audit) is a separate later dispatch and is NOT covered here.\n\n### Trigger disposition (all four, explicitly)\n- (1) Staleness — NEVER FIRED. Builder plan 07:09:03Z, position checkpoint 07:10, result 07:11:36Z. Total elapsed ~2.5 min against a ~10-15 min expected cadence. Liveness independently corroborated before any judgement (PVi7 lesson): #279 lock held by store identity pp3g-lPgz-verification-task-baseline-confirmation-for-a-re-df62, position stream advancing, artifacts consistent. No absence call was warranted at any point. WZSE lesson not engaged — the builder outran the staleness window entirely.\n- (2) Position-vs-artifact mismatch — CHECKED ALL FIVE, NONE FOUND. Detail below.\n- (3) Reviewer disagreement — none observed.\n- (4) Orchestrator request — none received.\n\n### Architectural Assessment\n- [OK] Criterion 1 — INDEPENDENTLY CONFIRMED. /tmp/toolregistry-venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages/toolregistry/integrations/mcp/connection.py:106 is 'except Exception:' — bare catch-all, no failure-class branch. Builder's claim exact.\n- [OK] Criterion 2 — INDEPENDENTLY CONFIRMED. _call_persistent spans exactly connection.py:97-111 (def at 97; final retry return at 111; line 112 blank; next def _call_per_request at 113). Builder's body enumeration verified line-for-line: lock 101/108, _ensure_connected 102, try 103, first call 105, except Exception 106, logger.warning telemetry 107, _connect 109, single retry 111. All correct.\n- [OK] Criterion 3 — INDEPENDENTLY CONFIRMED. integration.py:323 is 'connection = MCPConnectionManager(' — hardcoded constructor, no factory/injection/hook. Builder's secondary citation 'import at :22' also verified: integration.py:22 is 'from .connection import MCPConnectionManager'.\n- [OK] Criterion 4 — INDEPENDENTLY CONFIRMED. mcp/client/session.py:1110 is: raise RuntimeError(f'Invalid structured content returned by tool {name}: {error}') from error — verbatim, character-exact to the claim.\n- [OK] Version pins — INDEPENDENTLY CONFIRMED via a channel the builder did not use (dist-info directory listing, not importlib.metadata): toolregistry-0.15.0.dist-info/ and mcp-2.0.0.dist-info/ both present. The version-bound premise of #279 holds.\n- [OK] Criterion 5 — CONSISTENT, corroborated but not independently re-executed. The apparent tension (criterion text says '1 proxy'; builder reports proxies=2) is NOT a divergence. Validated two ways: (a) harness arithmetic phase_b2_poc.py:93, persistent = max(0, len(pids) - 1), so pids=2 yields persistent_proxies=1; and :97, reconnect_fired = len(pids) > 2, so False at pids=2; (b) report.md:327 frames the ORIGINAL baseline in the builder's exact words: 'Proxy processes | 2 = registration temp + 1 persistent'. The builder reconciled correctly rather than hand-waving. The pass predicate at :108-113 (spawns==1 and not pids>2 and schema_validation_failures>=1, AND error_preserved) is satisfied by the reported values.\n- [OK] Criterion 5 numbers match the recorded baseline on every criterion dimension. B2 vs report.md:326-331 — spawns=1, proxies=2/persistent=1, reconnect=False, schema_validation_failures=1, error_preserved=True, ErrorResult verbatim: all match. B2b vs report.md:355 and :358 — spawns=1, proxies=2, reconnect=False, schema_validation_failures=2, and the full flag set (pass, preabsorb_interception_fired, add1_error_preserved, warm_add_error_preserved, other_tool_success all True): all match.\n- [OK] Affirmative authenticity signal for criterion 5. The latency deltas DIVERGE from report.md while the criterion dimensions match: builder reports B2 delta_ms=1630 (report: 1830/1814/1799), B2b add=87 (report: 119), warm add=8 (report: 9), multiply=5 (report: 7). Fabrication by transcription from report.md would have reproduced the report's values exactly; independent variance confined to the non-criterion dimension is positive evidence of genuine fresh execution. Same order of magnitude throughout — no anomaly.\n- [OK] Repo hygiene claim verified. Builder asserted 'no repo files modified'; git status --porcelain shows only .crosslink/.last-hydrated-ref (sync metadata) and untracked .kickoff-session. No commit was made against #279 — correct for a read-only verification task.\n\n### Process Assessment\n- [OK] Workflow followed. plan -> position checkpoint -> result on #279, each with per-criterion file:line citations. The position stream was durable and legible; no reconstruction needed.\n- [OK] Claim discipline good. The builder cited file:line for every criterion rather than asserting bare verdicts, and volunteered the proxies=2 reconciliation instead of silently reporting '1 proxy' to match the criterion text. That is the behaviour the reasoning-certainty rule is meant to produce.\n- [OK/CONCERN] Reasoning-certainty (AGENTS.md) only partially satisfied. WHY/WHAT/HOW-CERTAIN are present and well-evidenced. WHAT-NOT-TESTED is ABSENT — the result declares 'BASELINE CONFIRMED' with no negative-space clause. It does not state that criterion 5's fresh run output was not preserved, nor that criteria 1-4 are single-version point reads with no cross-version differential. Per AGENTS.md this is the sharpest required element of a cross-role claim, and the #279 result crosses into Orchestrator decision-making.\n- [CONCERN] Criterion 5 evidence is testimonial, not durable — playbook §5.9 / #271. The harness writes to TRACKED log paths; the builder restored them byte-identical (sha256-verified) after the runs. Repo hygiene was preserved, but the consequence is that the fresh 2026-08-08 run output survives ONLY as prose transcription in the #279 comment. The committed logs under logs/ and logs/n3/ are the ORIGINAL runs, not this re-validation. I could not independently re-derive criterion 5 from any artifact in git. Criteria 1-4 are fully re-derivable (I re-derived all four); criterion 5 rests on builder testimony corroborated by consistency, which is materially weaker. This was a genuine dilemma the builder resolved reasonably — the right resolution was a third option (write to a NEW path and commit), not overwriting tracked baselines.\n- [CONCERN] #279 criterion 2 text is mis-specified — a defect in the TRIGGER, not in the builder's work. The criterion reads: _call_persistent still spans connection.py:97-111 with the same body (backoff/lock/telemetry/retry count). There is no backoff in that body. I grepped connection.py for sleep|backoff|retry|RETRY: the sole match is the line-107 logger.warning telemetry string. The body has a lock, telemetry, and a single unconditional immediate retry — no delay of any kind. The builder correctly enumerated the real body and did not claim backoff exists, but it also did not flag the discrepancy. Left unfixed, a future re-validator will search for a non-existent element and either mis-fail criterion 2 or waste a cycle.\n\n### Systemic Risks Identified\n- Re-validation triggers can rot in their own text. — #279 exists precisely because private-internal coupling makes the report 'read as current while potentially being void'. A criterion that names a non-existent code element (backoff) is that same failure class one level up: the trigger reads as precise while being partly unverifiable. — Mitigation: criterion text should QUOTE the code, not paraphrase it; correct criterion 2 to 'lock/telemetry/single-immediate-retry, no backoff'.\n- Fast, correct completions receive the least verification. — The builder finished in ~2.5 min, inside every staleness window, so the in-flight monitoring apparatus had no opportunity to engage. Phase-1 value here came entirely from claim-vs-artifact re-derivation, not from liveness monitoring. A wrong-but-fast builder would likewise be caught only by re-derivation. — Mitigation: keep Phase-1's mandate explicitly DUAL (staleness AND independent re-derivation); if it degrades into a liveness-only watchdog, fast-completion tasks become unverified by construction.\n- 'Restore the tracked baseline' silently destroys new evidence. — Harnesses that write to committed log paths force a choice between polluting baselines and discarding fresh evidence. This recurs on every re-run of this suite, and each recurrence yields a testimonial-only result. — Mitigation: parameterise the harness log destination (run-scoped subdirectory, e.g. logs/revalidation-DATE/) so fresh runs are committable without touching baselines.\n\n### Recommendations\n1. Re-run criterion 5 with run-scoped log output and COMMIT the logs (e.g. logs/revalidation-2026-08-08/) — converts the one testimonial criterion into a re-derivable artifact and satisfies §5.9/#271. Priority: MEDIUM (correctness is not in doubt; auditability is).\n2. Correct #279 criterion 2's parenthetical to name the actual body elements and explicitly state 'no backoff' — prevents a guaranteed future mis-verification. Priority: MEDIUM-HIGH (cheap, and the trigger is long-lived).\n3. Require a WHAT-NOT-TESTED clause on verification results that gate Orchestrator decisions — here it should state that criterion 5's fresh output was not preserved and that no cross-version differential was performed. Priority: MEDIUM.\n4. Do NOT close #279 on this baseline. It is a standing trigger; the builder correctly left it open. Closure would discard the re-validation mechanism. Priority: HIGH (guard against a well-intentioned cleanup pass).\n\n### Phase-1 Confirmation\nThe builder's per-criterion PASS/FAIL table is CONFIRMED against source evidence. Criteria 1-4: independently re-derived from primary source by this auditor, exact. Criterion 5: consistent with harness logic and the recorded baseline, corroborated by non-criterion latency variance, but not independently re-executed and not durably archived. NO divergence between the builder's durable positions and artifact evidence was found at any checkpoint. Certainty: criteria 1-4 PROVEN (direct re-read); criterion 5 EVIDENCE-BASED, NOT PROVEN (testimonial plus consistency corroboration). WHAT-NOT-TESTED for this audit: I did not re-execute the B2/B2b harness, did not diff toolregistry 0.15.0 / mcp 2.0.0 against any prior version, and did not inspect the builder's worktree filesystem (cross-worktree access blocked by design). Phase 1 closed.","created_at":"2026-08-08T07:17:28.534698393Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:52vyevofB+6K+bUG9ItpK6nRzMTdJkxcF7vDSwp2+pU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/gT8cmyhi1xAFU4gh0VAwmOFvbmLC4OkC/rvbR/setoAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAJoRpl2Mib9N7dLKyuAUBmfiuQiFV0U2ubwQz1zSFH0yRLenX/xU7Q8MjErq3R9DKVNjlaBto5Q39X8pSdmMNAQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:52vyevofB+6K+bUG9ItpK6nRzMTdJkxcF7vDSwp2+pU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/gT8cmyhi1xAFU4gh0VAwmOFvbmLC4OkC/rvbR/setoAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQM45rq7+TiDeebiR9BZPpkCRLgwgW16V6sJGIO3iIL9DFzAoPdAlAAace56q2pcNHoH2qqayj9/dul4PTvg8+wc="}
